course: dictionary
lesson: 4774
title: The hryvnia, Ukraine's money
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The hryvnia is the money of Ukraine. The money a country uses is called its currency, and the hryvnia is Ukraine's currency, just as the pound is Britain's and the dollar is America's.
explain: «A 100-hryvnia note from Gran in Kyiv buys crisps in Kyiv, but a London shop will not take it.» The clue is in the end of the sentence: London shops take pounds, so you must first swap the hryvnia at a bank or exchange shop.
explain: One hryvnia is made of 100 kopiyky. Its sign is ₴ and its short code is UAH. When you meet a new money word in maths or geography, ask: what country uses it, and what is its currency?
fact: The hryvnia is the currency of Ukraine.
fact: One hryvnia is made of 100 kopiyky.
fact: The sign for the hryvnia is ₴, and its short code is UAH.
fact: «Ukrainian hryvnia» and «100 hryvnias» show how the word is used; hryvnias is the plural.
fact: The hryvnia was a silver unit in Kyivan Rus, and the modern hryvnia was introduced in 1996.
exercise: «A 100-hryvnia note buys crisps in Kyiv.» What is a hryvnia? | A kind of cold weather | A famous bridge over the river | *The money of Ukraine | A type of bread from Kyiv
exercise: What is the short code for the hryvnia? | HRY | *UAH | KYV | UKR
exercise: How many kopiyky make one hryvnia? | 10 | *100 | 50 | 1000
test: Why will a London shop not take a 100-hryvnia note? | Because London shops only take euros | *Because London shops take pounds, so you must swap it first | Because the note is too old | Because the note is made of silver
test: Which sign stands for the hryvnia? | € | £ | *₴ | ¥
exam: «Every country chooses its own money, called its currency.» What does currency mean? | *The money a country uses | A bank in the capital city | A coin from a country's history | A country's flag and its symbols
